course: dictionary
lesson: 10710
title: Untouched
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Untouched means not touched, not handled or not used. Look at the parts of the word: un- means not, and touched means touched. The words around it tell you which meaning fits: food nobody has eaten, a place people have not changed, or a house the fire did not harm.
explain: «On his tenth birthday Corey sits by the phone all afternoon, cake untouched.» Corey is not eating his birthday cake. He is waiting for a call and is probably upset, so untouched can also mean not affected emotionally.
explain: «A tornado... may destroy one street while leaving the next one untouched.» Here untouched means not damaged. Check by swapping in your meaning: "leaving the next one not damaged" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Untouched means not touched, not handled or not used.
fact: «Untouched» can mean not damaged or changed, as in an «untouched rainforest».
fact: «Untouched» can also mean not affected emotionally.
fact: «Tutankhamun» was pharaoh as a boy of about nine and died at about nineteen; his tomb was found almost untouched in 1922.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, so unhappy means not happy, and untouched means not touched.
exercise: «Her dinner lay untouched on the plate.» What does untouched show about her? | She is very busy cooking | *She is upset or unwell | She is hungry and wants more | She has just finished eating
exercise: «The rainforest is still untouched by people.» What does untouched mean here? | Very wet and muddy | *Not changed by people | Covered in snow | Full of loud sounds
exercise: «The house was untouched by the fire.» What does untouched mean here? | Painted a new colour | Burned to the ground | *Not damaged | Moved to a new place
test: «Tutankhamun's tomb was found almost untouched in 1922.» What does untouched mean here? | Very large | Wet with rain | Painted bright gold | *Not disturbed or changed
test: «Jake heard the bad news, but he seemed untouched by it.» What does untouched mean here? | Hungry again | *Not upset by it | Lost in thought | Covered in mud
exam: «Corey's cake lay untouched all afternoon.» Why did Corey not eat it? | It was too big to eat | He hates cake | He ate it all before the party | *He was waiting and worried, and not thinking about food
